<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Frederick Charles of Hesse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Frederick Charles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> was a German prince, brother-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a>, who was elected King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> by the Finnish parliament on 9 October 1918, when the Whites hoped for German protection against Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. He never travelled to Finland, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s defeat he renounced the throne on 14 December 1918, opening the way to the Finnish republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-frederick-charles-of-hesse.jpg" alt="Prince Frederick Charles of Hesse" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hessenin_prnssi_Friedrich_Karl_-_Prince_Frederick_Charles_of_Hesse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A German prince, <b>Frederick Charles of Hesse</b>, was elected king in October 1918 but renounced the throne after Germany’s defeat, and the constitution of July 1919 made Finland a republic with K. J. Ståhlberg as its first president.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Republic of Finland · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>…turned to elected kings: Norway’s parliament chose Prince Carl of Denmark as Haakon VII in 1905, Finland’s elected <b>Prince Frederick Charles of Hesse</b> in 1918, though he never reigned, and at independence in 1957 Malaya’s Conference of Rulers began to elect a federal king, the Yang di-Pertuan Agong.</blockquote><a href="/government/elective-monarchy">Elective monarchy · Through History</a></li><li><blockquote>On 9 October 1918 a rump parliament, without the Social Democrats, elected <b>Prince Frederick Charles of Hesse</b> as king of Finland.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-finland-1918">Kingdom of Finland (1918)</a></li></ul></section>
